# ControlRig And AnimBP MCP Learning Workflow

Use this workflow for UnrealMCP work involving Control Rig, Animation
Blueprints, AnimGraph nodes, state machines, Post Process AnimBPs, pose
sampling, or animation-related MCP API gaps.

The goal is to prevent failed "try Python first" loops around editor-protected
AnimGraph and ControlRig internals. Runtime/gameplay code is out of scope unless
the user explicitly changes that boundary.

## Read Order

After the repository bootstrap, read these files before planning or editing
ControlRig/AnimBP MCP behavior:

1. `Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_failure_patterns.md`
2. `Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_api_map.md`
3. `Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_command_surface_gap_analysis.md`
4. `Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_api_authority_matrix.md`
5. `Docs/Research/controlrig_authoring_tool_plan.md` when the request involves
   recipe-driven ControlRig creation, a standalone ControlRig editor tool, or
   authored assets that must avoid UnrealMCP dependencies
6. `Docs/Research/controlrig_stable_authoring_execution_plan.md` when the
   request needs stable from-scratch ControlRig generation or a handoff plan
   for the next implementation section
7. `Docs/Research/inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded_design.md` when
   the request involves notifies, curves, sync markers, Montage sections, slots,
   or branching-point metadata
8. `Docs/Research/ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant_design.md` when the
   request needs new sample state-machine states, transitions, or asset players
9. `Docs/Research/ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver_design.md` when
   the request needs sample AnimBP `Speed`, `Direction`, `IsInAir`,
   `Acceleration`, or `IsAccelerating` EventGraph driving for locomotion
10. `Docs/Research/extend_anim_node_runtime_mapping_design.md` when selected
   node attribution, compiled mapping, or PoseWatch capture fails for a node
   class
11. `Docs/Research/ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample_design.md` when a
   safe sample AnimBP needs a new ControlRig AnimGraph node
12. `Docs/Research/inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded_design.md` when
   the request needs PhysicsAsset bodies, constraints, limits, drives, or
   profiles
13. `Docs/Research/create_anim_blueprint_sample_design.md` when a sample AnimBP
   must be created from a Skeleton or SkeletalMesh
14. `Docs/Research/ensure_controlrig_sample_asset_design.md` when a safe
    sample ControlRig asset must be created or seeded
15. `Docs/Research/linked_anim_graph_layer_sample_authoring_design.md` when
    sample linked Anim Graph, linked Anim Layer, or Sub Anim Instance authoring
    is requested
16. `Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_request_routing_checklist.md`
17. `Docs/Tools/anim_controlrig_tools.md`
18. `Docs/Research/controlrig_solver_intent_validation_design.md` when the
    request asks for solver planning without a live sample
19. `Docs/Tools/node_tools.md` for full command schemas when needed
20. `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/studies/stackobot-animation/stackobot-animation-doc-index.md` only when the request is StackOBot-specific or needs historical animation-study evidence

## Scope

Allowed by default:

- read-only inspection of AnimBP, AnimGraph, state-machine, ControlRig, and
  SkeletalMeshComponent animation state through existing MCP commands;
- sample-only or temp-only asset work under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or
  `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`;
- editor-only UnrealMCP bridge changes when a documented API gap blocks a
  concrete MCP task;
- docs, research notes, wrapper schemas, and verification artifacts.

Not allowed by default:

- gameplay/runtime module changes;
- final project asset mutation outside sample/temp roots;
- generic Python edits to protected AnimGraph node/link/pin state;
- broad Montage, notify, curve, or animation asset internals probing through
  ad hoc Python;
- saving, deleting, renaming, or overwriting original animation assets without a
  specific user-approved plan.

## Authority Rule

Before chaining ControlRig or AnimBP MCP commands, use
`Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_api_authority_matrix.md` to choose one write
authority for the current target and operation. Inspectors and validators are
not writers, high-level `ensure_*` commands own only their documented sample
topology, and low-level `add_*`/`set_*` writers own only their reviewed
sample/temp edit class.

Stop the chain and inspect the target before continuing when a writer response
reports `success=false`, `partial_target_modified=true`,
`compile_succeeded=false`, or `save_succeeded=false`.

## Planning Rule

Classify the request before choosing a tool:

| Request shape | First route |
| --- | --- |
| "What nodes/state/links/settings exist?" | `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology`, `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings`, or `inspect_anim_state_machine_transitions` |
| "Does this ControlRig gate respond?" | `controlrig_direct_gate_probe` first, then same-instance AnimGraph proof if needed |
| "Did this AnimGraph node change the pose?" | `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose` dry-run, check `mapping_support`, then `mode=pose_watch_capture` when a live target exists |
| "Assign AnimBP to a SkeletalMeshComponent template" | `set_skeletal_mesh_component_anim_defaults` |
| "Make a safe sample Post Process change" | `ensure_postprocess_anim_demo_variant`, `ensure_anim_graph_modify_bone_demo`, or related sample-only command |
| "Force ControlRig driver inputs in a sample" | `ensure_controlrig_forced_driver_animbp` or `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` |
| "Read ControlRig RigVM graph nodes, pins, links, unit script structs, proposed link feasibility, or pin-default feasibility" | use `inspect_controlrig_rigvm_topology`; for proposed links, follow with `validate_controlrig_rigvm_links`; for proposed/default pins, follow with `validate_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults`; use `/ControlRigModules/Modules/AddControl.AddControl` as a known UE 5.6.1 positive read-only fixture when a link/default-validating example is needed |
| "Write reviewed RigVM links or pin defaults on a sample/temp ControlRig" | validate first, then use `add_controlrig_rigvm_links` or `set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults`; stop for Ieta review before non-sample targets, cast-node creation, arbitrary graph authoring, or original asset mutation |
| "Add a ControlRig AnimGraph node to a safe sample" | use `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`; stop for Ieta review only when the request needs behavior outside its sample/temp scope |
| "Read PhysicsAsset bodies or constraints" | read `inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded_design.md`, then stop for Ieta review before C++ |
| "Create a sample AnimBP from a skeleton or mesh" | read `create_anim_blueprint_sample_design.md`, then stop for Ieta review before C++ |
| "Create a sample/temp BlendSpace variant or edit speed axis/sample coordinates" | use the planner/job-contract `blendspace_sample_variant` route or `ensure_blendspace_sample_variant` under `/Game/_MCP_Sample`/`/Game/_MCP_Temp`; verify with `sample_blendspace_runtime_pose_grid`; stop for Ieta review before original BlendSpace mutation |
| "Update AnimBP Speed/Direction/IsInAir/Acceleration/IsAccelerating from pawn data for locomotion" | use `ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver` for the sample/temp locomotion EventGraph driver; chain with `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant` when states or BlendSpacePlayer inputs also need authoring |
| "Create an automatic sample locomotion AnimBP" | use the planner/job-contract `anim_bp_locomotion_sample_pipeline`, which runs `ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver` then `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant` on one sample/temp target; stop for Ieta review before gait, turn-in-place, aim-offset, warping, or original asset mutation |
| "Create or seed a sample ControlRig asset" | use `ensure_controlrig_sample_asset` for empty, preview-only, bounded preview-hierarchy, bounded direct-curve, direct-null, null-transform, scalar-control, transform-control, direct control shape metadata, named-parent, or allowlisted single-instance ControlRig event-unit samples; use separate writer commands for reviewed sample/temp RigVM links/defaults; stop for Ieta review before arbitrary script structs, variables, functions, comments, reroutes, dispatch nodes, exposed pins, graph replacement, or units beyond the approved event-unit allowlist |
| "Plan stable ControlRig recipe inputs from a skeletal mesh or skeleton" | use `profile_controlrig_skeleton` for read-only bounded bone, parent-chain, humanoid alias, missing/ambiguous alias, and controls-only preset evidence before hand-writing recipes; do not build assets or add solver units in Phase 1 |
| "Compile stable ControlRig recipe planning from a skeleton profile" | use `compile_controlrig_profile_recipe` to produce deterministic controls-only preset request or dry-run recipe JSON; ambiguous required aliases require explicit `bone_overrides`; do not build assets or add solver units in Phase 2 |
| "Build or retry a stable ControlRig recipe" | inspect Phase 3 report fields from `validate_controlrig_recipe`, `dry_run_controlrig_recipe`, or `build_controlrig_recipe`: `planned_writes`, `performed_writes`, `skipped_writes`, `reused_items`, `cleanup_suggestions`, and `next_action`; if `partial_target_modified=true`, inspect or clean up the sample/temp target before another writer |
| "Verify the first stable Piper fixture" | use `Docs/Research/fixtures/controlrig_piper_stable_prototype_recipe.json` with `smoke_controlrig_stable_fixture.py`; it builds only `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype`, keeps `save=false`, and checks compile/dependency audit/report evidence |
| "Add pose-changing ControlRig solver units" | read `Docs/Research/controlrig_solver_unit_allowlist_research.md`; first candidate is `FRigUnit_SetTransform`, but implementation remains Ieta-review gated and must prove pin-default feasibility, compile, dependency audit, readback, direct solve behavior, and cleanup |
| "Plan solver intent without a sample" | use the UnrealMCP-native `validate_controlrig_solver_intents` route only for sampleless solver intent evidence under `validation_only_no_sample`; it rejects build/save/execute requests and does not approve solver unit expansion |
| "Bind the stable ControlRig fixture into a sample AnimBP" | read `Docs/Research/controlrig_animbp_binding_proof_design.md` and `Docs/Analysis/controlrig_stable_authoring_phase6_handoff.md`, then use `smoke_controlrig_animbp_binding_bridge.py --stable-fixture` only against a running UE bridge; this binds sample/temp targets and applies only reviewed stable fixture input defaults such as `PiperStable_GlobalStableGate_CTRL=1.0` |
| "Create linked AnimBP composition with an existing compatible linked AnimBP" | use the planner/job-contract linked graph route or `ensure_linked_anim_graph_sample_variant` for the sample/temp Linked Anim Graph MVP; stop for Ieta review before Linked Anim Layer/interface creation, Sub Anim Instance wrappers, or arbitrary graph insertion |
| "Create/change original AnimBP graph behavior" | stop for Ieta review and an explicit mutation plan |

## Evidence Ladder

Prefer the weakest evidence that answers the question, then climb only when the
request needs stronger proof:

1. Static topology/settings read.
2. Direct transient ControlRig solve.
3. Runtime state/property response.
4. Live component final-pose tick delta.
5. Same-instance PoseWatch pre/post capture.
6. Sample-only authoring plus compile/save/readback.
7. New editor-only C++ bridge command.

Do not present lower evidence as higher evidence. A direct transient ControlRig
solve does not prove the same node evaluated inside a live AnimBP. A final
SkeletalMeshComponent tick delta does not prove one selected node caused the
delta.

## Escalation

Ieta review is required before Tivret implements any of these:

- new UnrealMCP C++ command;
- non-sample asset mutation;
- save/delete/rename/overwrite operation;
- broad animation metadata probing;
- runtime/gameplay code request;
- change that adds a project dependency on the UnrealMCP plugin.

Tivret may continue without another user round trip when the work stays within
docs, read-only MCP inspection, or sample/temp editor-only tooling already
covered by this workflow.

## Completion Gate

For docs-only work:

- link the new material from the relevant index;
- keep the rule in Git-tracked Markdown;
- run a basic markdown/link sanity check when practical.

For ControlRig/AnimBP Python wrapper, server prompt, analysis audit, or tool
documentation changes, prefer the aggregate filesystem-only gate:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\controlrig_animbp_mcp_release_gate.py
```

This gate runs Python compilation, server import, MCP parity audit/tests,
Blueprint/AnimBP planner/job/executor tests, planner-driven authoring smoke,
ControlRig/AnimBP surface audit/tests, and ControlRig/AnimBP semantic audit/tests
for sample writer compile/save, partial-target response markers, stable
ControlRig authoring transaction markers, stable fixture roots/save/dependency
audit settings, and static `UnrealMCP` -> `UnrealMCPControlRigToolsEditor`
dependency strings.
It intentionally does not launch Unreal Editor, build C++, or mutate assets.

For a narrow Python wrapper smoke when the aggregate gate is not available:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\node_tools.py tools\blueprint_tools.py
```

For C++ bridge changes:

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Build\BatchFiles\Build.bat' MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development -Project="$Project" -WaitMutex
```
